{"id": "unknown-2026-10-20-010", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Taiwanese PV manufacturers create back-contact TOPCon alliance", "content": "<p>Taiwan’s Industrial Technology Research Institute (ITRI) has established a photovoltaic technology alliance with seven domestic companies to develop a local supply chain for tunnel oxide passivated contact back-contact (TBC) solar cells. The institute is also promoting a laser-assisted silver-coated copper electrode technology that could reduce solar cell production costs by 8%.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/20/taiwanese-pv-manufacturers-create-back-contact-topc", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/20/taiwanese-pv-manufacturers-create-back-contact-topcon-alliance/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "gcl-2026-10-20-011", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": ["gcl"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "GCL Technology moves to buy LFP cathode maker from founder’s group", "content": "<p>Chinese polysilicon producer GCL Technology has signed a non-binding memorandum of understanding to buy a controlling stake in an lithium iron phosphate (LFP) cathode manufacturer owned by its chairman’s family group for about CNY 2.5 billion ($374.3 million), as losses in its core polysilicon business continue.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/20/gcl-technology-moves-to-buy-lfp-cathode-maker-from-founders-group/\">GCL Technology moves to buy LFP cathode maker from ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/20/gcl-technology-moves-to-buy-lfp-cathode-maker-from-founders-group/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-20-012", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "U.S. startup launches 200 kWh flywheel energy storage pilot", "content": "<p>Individual Pulsar units expected to achieve 500 kWh capacity with 125 kW discharge rate.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/20/qnetic-testing-flywheel-to-compete-with-lithium-ion-for-grid-connected-energy-storage/\">U.S. startup launches 200 kWh flywheel energy storage pilot</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/20/qnetic-testing-flywheel-to-compete-with-lithium-ion-for-grid-connected-energy-storage/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-20-013", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Elevated agrivoltaics for olive cultivation", "content": "<p>Spanish olive oil producer Acesur has started building a 3.65 MW agrivoltaic plant featuring elevated solar modules above an existing olive grove in Jaén, Spain. The project will include a 3 MWh battery storage system and supply electricity to the company's nearby packaging facility.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/20/elevated-agrivoltaics-for-olive-cultivation/\">Elevated agrivoltaics for olive cultivation</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/20/elevated-agrivoltaics-for-olive-cultivation/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-20-014", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Poland eases connection rules for home batteries up to 2.2x PV power", "content": "<p>Polish prosumers will be able to connect batteries with up to 2.2 times the rated power of their PV systems without the storage counting toward installed capacity, under amended rules that take effect Dec. 1.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/20/poland-eases-connection-rules-for-home-batteries-up-to-2-2x-pv-power/\">Poland eases connection rules for home batteries up to 2.2x PV power</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.<", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/20/poland-eases-connection-rules-for-home-batteries-up-to-2-2x-pv-power/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-20-015", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "New framework prioritizes fire protection measures for BIPV façades", "content": "<p>Researchers in China and Italy have developed a framework to assess fire risks in building-integrated photovoltaic (BIPV) façades, identifying electrical and material-related hazards as key factors. Their analysis highlights rapid shutdown, ignition prevention and fire-spread suppression as priority safety measures.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/20/new-framework-prioritizes-fire-protection-measures-for-bipv-facades/\">New framework prioritizes fire protection mea", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/20/new-framework-prioritizes-fire-protection-measures-for-bipv-facades/", "type": "rss"}]}
